Iridescence derives from Tint my Gnome and Tinted Shell by PakoVM.
GTK @import integration was inspired by pull request #2 by snelbinderr:
https://github.com/pakovm-git/Tint-my-Gnome/pull/2

The light palette in themes/shell-light.css was supplied by the user from a tinted
Luminus theme. Its original notice credits Red Hat, Inc. (2009, 2015) and Intel
Corporation (2009), under GNU LGPL version 2.1. That notice is preserved in the
source file. The palette's layout declarations are excluded from generated CSS.

The Tinted Shell GPL version 3 license is included in LICENSE. Original source
notices are retained in themes/. Iridescence is distributed as a GNOME Shell extension.
